>> title: Smoked Brisket
>> category: Smoked & Grilled
>> tags: beef, brisket, barbecue, smoker, low and slow
>> counters: Smokehouse
>> aka: brisket, sliced brisket, lean, moist, fatty, flat, point, packer brisket, bbq brisket, barbeque brisket
>> servings: 12
>> time: 16 hr
>> slack: narrow — 203°F and a probe that slides through the flat, not the clock: pulled at 190°F the brisket is tough for good
>> pairs-with: barbecue-sauce, coleslaw

Bring the #smoker{} to 250°F (120°C) over post oak and hold it there.

>> step: trim to a 1/4-in fat cap, season
Trim @whole packer brisket{12%lb}(5.4 kg) to an even 1/4-in fat cap and season it all over with @kosher salt{3%Tbs} and @coarse black pepper{3%Tbs}(16 mesh), and nothing else.

>> step: stir a spritz
Stir @cider vinegar{1%cup}(240 mL) and @water{1%cup}(240 mL) together in a spray bottle.

>> step: smoke 250°F (120°C) 8 hr, to 165°F (74°C)
Smoke @&(~2)seasoned brisket{} fat side up, spritzing it hourly with @&(~1)spritz{}, for ~smoke{8%hr}, to 165°F (74°C) and a set bark that will not smudge under a thumb.

>> step: wrap, back in 4 hr, to 203°F (95°C)
Wrap @&(~1)smoked brisket{} tight in #butcher paper{} with @beef tallow{2%Tbs} and return it to the smoker for ~smoke{4%hr}, to 203°F (95°C), until a probe goes through the flat like warm butter.

>> step: rest 2 hr, slice pencil-thick
Rest @&(~1)wrapped brisket{} still wrapped for ~rest{2%hr}, then slice it pencil-thick across the grain — the flat for lean, the point for moist — and finish with @flaky salt{1%tsp}.
